  "boundaries": [
    "Scenario conditions are explicit assumptions, not forecasts or likelihood estimates.",
    "Stress-test passes do not imply approval, certification, or recommendation.",
    "Ordering changes, threshold breaches, and score swings are surfaced for accountable review rather than resolved automatically.",
    "Uncertainty bounds and sensitivity tests remain available from v2.4.0 and do not convert uncertainty into certainty.",
    "Process confidence describes documentation and analysis coverage, not probability of correctness.",
    "Decision Object promotion is additive; Decision Packet 2.0 remains supported and reversible.",
    "Browser-local handoffs are not remote API delivery.",
    "Human review remains required before approval, publication, or consequential use.",
    "Decision Studio does not execute Lab experiments or Workbench computations; it requests, receives, links, and reviews source-owned artifacts.",
    "A successful handoff receipt confirms contract and fingerprint checks only; it is not scientific validation, engineering verification, approval, or recommendation.",
    "Site Intelligence context remains source-owned observation/context and is not rewritten as a causal claim.",
    "Freshness, observation time, geography, methodology, and limitations remain visible in every attached context snapshot.",
    "Scenario links are explicit reviewer-supplied relationships; they do not change scenario scores or imply likelihood.",
    "A Site Intelligence context receipt confirms contract and fingerprint integrity only; it is not truth verification, approval, or recommendation.",
    "Dependency edges represent explicit or structural relationships, not causal proof.",
    "Node degree and fan-out are structural diagnostics, not importance, truth, confidence, or priority scores.",
    "Change-impact reachability creates a review queue; it does not automatically invalidate a scenario, recommendation, or decision."
  ],
